      <title>✖️ The Hustle Miniso puts roughly 100 new products on its shelves every week. Th</title>
      <link>https://t.me/KissmeBabyFeedTwitter/24391</link>
      <description>&lt;div class="tgme_widget_message_text js-message_text" dir="auto"&gt;&lt;tg-emoji emoji-id="5355148941878900494"&gt;&lt;i class="emoji" style="background-image:url('//telegram.org/img/emoji/40/E29C96.png')"&gt;&lt;b&gt;✖️&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/tg-emoji&gt; &lt;a href="https://x.com/TheHustle/status/2116957226476916933" onclick="return confirm('Open this link?\n\n'+this.href);" rel="noopener" target="_blank"&gt;The Hustle&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Miniso puts roughly 100 new products on its shelves every week.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The company calls it the "7-Eleven philosophy." Inventory turns over in about 21 days, so what's on the shelf today may not be there next month.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Why move that fast? Low prices were part of Miniso's edge, but a low price is easy to copy.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;And it keeps speeding up. By 2025, Miniso was launching around 1,600 new SKUs a month globally, nearly three times the roughly 550 it launched in 2021.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;It's working in the US, too. In 2026, the National Retail Federation ranked Miniso the fastest-growing retailer in America, ahead of Dick's, Five Below and Primark.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Its US sales jumped roughly 53% to $466 million.&lt;/div&gt;</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://t.me/KissmeBabyFeedTwitter/24391</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 22:43:18 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
