    <item>
      <title>✖️ The Hustle A Toy Story villain out-trended Toy Story itself in China. Miniso </title>
      <link>https://t.me/KissmeBabyFeedTwitter/24386</link>
      <description>&lt;div class="tgme_widget_message_text js-message_text" dir="auto"&gt;&lt;tg-emoji emoji-id="5355148941878900494"&gt;&lt;i class="emoji" style="background-image:url('//telegram.org/img/emoji/40/E29C96.png')"&gt;&lt;b&gt;✖️&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/tg-emoji&gt; &lt;a href="https://x.com/TheHustle/status/2116687355734339886" onclick="return confirm('Open this link?\n\n'+this.href);" rel="noopener" target="_blank"&gt;The Hustle&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;A Toy Story villain out-trended Toy Story itself in China.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Miniso launched a Toy Story collection there, and one character quickly took off: Lotso.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Instead of guessing, Miniso tested him with customers. Shoppers voted on designs, and pre-sales told Miniso how much to stock. Chinese reporting says all four Lotso products in the pre-sale sold out.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Why did he hit so hard? Maybe because he was plush, strawberry-scented and cute, a perfect fit for the kind of stuff Miniso already sold.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;In China, Lotso became Strawberry Bear, with his own commercial plugging 13 different products.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;A second-tier character basically became his own brand.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;That's what licensed IP opened the door to: Miniso could bet on a bunch of characters and see what stuck.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Not bad for the villain from Toy Story 3.&lt;/div&gt;</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://t.me/KissmeBabyFeedTwitter/24386</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 06:42:04 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
